course: dictionary
lesson: 4722
title: Hopeful and its family
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hopeful is an adjective, a word that describes how someone feels or what something is like. «She was hopeful that her dog would come home.» The clue is that she believes good news will probably come, so hopeful means feeling that something good will probably happen.
explain: Hopeful can also describe a sign or a result. «A hopeful sign» gives you a reason to hope. In science, a «hopeful result» looks good, but it is not certain yet. Ask yourself: is this a feeling, or a reason for a feeling?
explain: Hopeful can also be a noun. «Olympic hopefuls» are people who are trying hard to win a place or a medal. Words that end in -ful are often describing words, so check the sentence to see whether the word is describing or naming someone.
fact: Hopeful is an adjective. Its noun form, a hopeful, means a person who hopes to win or succeed.
fact: The suffix -ful means full of, so hopeful means full of hope.
fact: The suffix -ful has one l: careful, hopeful, beautiful.
fact: The opposite of hopeful is hopeless, because -less means without.
fact: A silent e stays before an ending that starts with a consonant: hope, hopeful.
exercise: «She was hopeful that her dog would come home.» What does hopeful mean here? | Certain that nothing will ever change | Tired and sleepy | *Feeling that something good will probably happen | Angry with the dog
exercise: Which spelling means full of hope? | hopful | *hopeful | hopefal | hopefull
exercise: In «Olympic hopefuls», what are the hopefuls? | Pieces of hope | Judges who score the races | Medals won at the games | *People who hope to win or succeed
test: Which word is the opposite of hopeful? | Joyful | *Hopeless | Careful | Helpful
test: A «hopeful result» in science means the result: | Is finished and certain | Is a kind of number | *Looks good but is not sure yet | Has failed completely
exam: Fill in the blank: The team stayed ____ after a bad start, so they kept training hard. | *Hopeful | Useful | Careless | Hopeless
